# Database rules

Source: ADR-0006; `docs/architecture/ARCHITECTURE.md` §5.8, §7.

- Six schemas and four roles exactly as ADR-0006. Grants go through default privileges; never grant the app role access to `core`, `meta`, `snap` or `seed_meta`, and never give the reader role write access.
- No table in `agent` or `insights` before its owning contract freeze (CF-3, CF-5).
- Alembic is one linear history; files `NNNN_m<milestone>_<slug>.py`; every revision implements `downgrade()`. A merged revision is never edited.
- Migrations contain DDL and grants only — never business data (the seed owns data).
- Every destructive command calls the guards DG-1 to DG-5 in `cenomi.db.guards`. Never bypass or weaken a guard. (Checked: AT-M0-T02-07.)
- `make db-check` (alembic check + role verification) must be clean after `make db-upgrade`.
- Tests use `cenomi_test` or per-worker `cenomi_test_gw<N>`, never `cenomi_dev`.
